  "title": "The Rain-Sorting Rooftops",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "block-world chain reactions",
  "premise": "A block village wants to fill three decorative ponds, but one roof sends all toy rain beads into the first basin. As each basin reaches its marked level, a floating block tips a channel toward the next, ending with a row of tiny flags instead of an overflowing plaza.",
  "hook": "Every drop keeps choosing the same address.",
  "visible_action": "Beads roll down roofs; floats rise; channels tilt one after another; three ponds fill to marks; flags lift.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A sequence can redirect a flow when each stage is ready.",
  "gate": "Toy beads stand in for rain; model the mechanism consistently and avoid flood-control or water-safety claims.",
